{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_0113i3zHZRRSMEcAT1pzwnfo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **Q33: What is FlashAttention and how does it work?** (`answers/01-033-what-is-flashattention-and-how-does-it-work.md`).\n\n**Key content covered:**\n- **Concept:** IO-aware exact attention that tiles computation into SRAM to avoid O(N²) HBM traffic — no approximation\n- **Mechanism:** Three-phase standard attention's HBM bottleneck → FlashAttention's tiling + online softmax (Milakov/Gimelshein running-max trick) + backward recomputation; FA2 adds sequence-dim parallelism; FA3 targets H100 with async warp specialization + FP8\n- **Concrete numbers:** ~3–4× faster, O(N) vs O(N²) memory, enables 128K-token contexts on A100 80GB; adopted by vLLM, TGI, TensorRT-LLM\n- **Pitfalls caught:** FA ≠ approximate attention (common misconception); must explain *why* it's faster (HBM/SRAM bandwidth hierarchy, not FLOPs); must distinguish from KV cache (different optimization)\n- **Cross-links:** Q9 (KV cache), Q34 (memory-bounded inference), Q23 (GQA)\n\n16 items remain in the Next queue (Q34–Q48 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":325,"cache_read_input_tokens":57690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":325,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4025bd-fdd8-48d4-8d86-3e453c764244","uuid":"3d8ba055-12be-408b-9178-0a47e8c076d1"}
